{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963585,"nonce":"hnYKbnsFAgPleYan5ZQS6ZGeZUk=","title":"A Dynamic value returned from a function with a concrete return type is not unboxed","message":"Row: Issue5894.\n\n- tast/ast_lowering/infer.rs `infer_return_type_from_body` prefers an \"informative\" `return 0`\n  over `return e` with `e:Dynamic`; Haxe types the local function Dynamic. The lambda gets\n  `-\u003e i32` and returns the box pointer.\n- The Return lowering (ir/mir/stmt/statements.rs) unboxes Dynamic-\u003econcrete only for registers in\n  `boxed_value_regs`: `function h(d:Dynamic):Int return d;` returns the pointer.\n- With an explicit `:Dynamic` return, `eq\u003cT\u003e(1, dyn)` with T=Int compares 1 against the box.\n\nHazard: `Dynamic` is usually a decay; a box rule keyed on the declared type alone lost rows\nbefore (bugs_function_values_and_untyped_params_decayed_dynamic).","files":null}]}